      "message": "test(app): the wire laws stand between a wire cut and its NC text\n\nOn the combined #533/#534 head the wire post is real, so the wire\nclause now gates actual NC text: a clean punch is judged by the wire\nlaws and posts wire-iso.cps's golden byte-for-byte (the program is\nwritten, the not-judged line names the wire verdict); a die whose kerf\nburns the plate above its 12 mm opening streams like any wire cut but\npost_script refuses it by name (\"Die1: wire gouge: the kerf of move\n...\") and writes no NC file.\n\nRefs #534\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
